      "role": "user",
      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>Those are a good start, but they're a bit generic. I really want to lean into that \"gritty realism\" aspect. When people think of these types of urban crime dramas, they usually have a very specific vision of the demographics and the social dynamics at play. \n\nTo make it feel less like a template and more like a real show, can you flesh these out a bit more? For example, when you're thinking about the \"Corner Hustler\" or the \"Network Boss,\" what kind of ethnic backgrounds or specific cultural vibes are you seeing for them to make them feel like they actually belong in that neighborhood? And how would that contrast with the detectives?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
